    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d258">

                <pb facs="0536" n="440" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg440"/>

                <head>No. 256.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Bancroft.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-02-18"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 18,
                        1874</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 650.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I learn from a source entitled to respect
                    that a statement has been recently published by the Ulmer Schrellpost, and other
                    German newspapers, to the effect that one Rohrer, who nine years ago had been
                    convicted of a triple murder in the kingdom of Würtemberg, was now offered his
                    discharge upon the condition that he should emigrate to the United States.</p>
                <p>You will please make inquiries in the proper quarter to ascertain the truth of
                    this report, and if it should be verified on good authority you will represent
                    the matter to the proper authorities, and, on the part of the United States,
                    protest against the granting of pardons on these or similar conditions.</p>
                <p>I am. &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
